I misinterpreted the capital I (i) as a lowercase l (L), too.

You want EIbryxam, then. Or Eibryxam, or EIbry'am, or Eibry'em. In all
cases, the 'e' has to be capitalized to be stressed. Just capitalizing the
'i' makes an extra syllable: e-I-bry-xam.

stevo

